  "description": "KACYIA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H150 Cl6 Hf4 Nd4 O30. From the CIF bond table, Hf1 (Hf) has 6 O neighbors; Hf2 (Hf) has 6 O neighbors; Nd1 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Hf3 (Hf) has 6 O neighbors; Hf4 (Hf) has 6 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.382-4.278 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.33-126.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H150O30Cl6Nd4Hf4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
